{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RLSA-2026:98086","published":"2026-11-13T12:06:37.188502Z","modified":"2026-11-13T12:45:02.738446192Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-111943","CVE-2026-33818","CVE-2026-56853","CVE-2026-56862","CVE-2026-78667","CVE-2026-97031"],"summary":"Important: delve security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"Delve is a debugger for the Go programming language. The goal of the project is to provide a simple, full featured debugging tool for Go. Delve should be easy to invoke and easy to use. Chances are if you're using a debugger, things aren't going your way. With that in mind, Delve should stay out of your way as much as possible.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* encoding/asn1: golang: Go encoding/asn1: Denial of Service via excessive recursion in Unmarshal (CVE-2026-33818)\n\n* net/http: golang: Go net/http: Unencrypted HTTP/2 connections vulnerable to Denial of Service (CVE-2026-56853)\n\n* crypto/tls: golang: Golang crypto/tls: Denial of Service via indefinite KeyUpdate messages (CVE-2026-56862)\n\n* net/http: golang: golang: Denial of Service via crafted HTTP Range headers (CVE-2026-78667)\n\n* crypto/tls: golang: crypto/tls: Denial of Service via multiple ECH outer extension references (CVE-2026-97031)\n\n* crypto/x509: golang: crypto/x509: Man-in-the-middle attacks via untrusted intermediate certificates (CVE-2026-111943)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Update Delve to 1.27 [rhel-10] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-219317)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"delve","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/delve?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:1.27.2-3.el10_3"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf